VIEW: the in-game camera - a high orthographic three-quarter top-down view looking down at about 50 degrees, the same framing as ref_current_town_layout.png: the whole town visible at once, roads forming the cross, buildings readable from above with their roofs and front facades, like a polished mobile RPG town hub map.
TOWN CONTENT (keep the same town, only the art changes): ref_current_town_layout.png is the current in-game town seen from the game camera (dark, gloomy). Keep its layout and every facility:
- a cross-shaped main road: one long east-west street and one north-south street meeting at a central plaza;
- at the crossroads, the RIFT GATEWAY: a stone arch with a swirling glowing portal inside (the way to the dungeons);
- north side, left to right: the WAREHOUSE (big storehouse), a small open-air WEAPON MERCHANT STALL with an awning, a round STONE WELL, the BLACKSMITH forge (chimney, anvil, warm forge glow), and a fenced TRAINING GROUND with four straw training dummies;
- west of the plaza near the warehouse: the RUNE ALTAR, a carved standing stone with a glowing rune;
- south side: a row of four small SHOP HOUSES with colourful awnings (gamble shop, gem shop, rune shop, rune workshop);
- street lanterns along the roads, wooden fences along the north and south edges, trees all around the town;
- a few townsfolk NPCs standing at their shops (blacksmith, merchant, warehouse keeper, rune master, training instructor, shop keepers) and a couple of passers-by.
